IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cidra-types`
IMPORT `cidra-misrepresentation`
IMPORT `cidra-remedies`

-- Consumer Insurance (Disclosure and Representations) Act 2012 (UK) — THE
-- TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "A consumer made a misrepresentation before taking out insurance and has
--    made a claim. Does the Act apply; is it a qualifying misrepresentation,
--    and of which class; and what may the insurer do?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Misrepresentation case` HAS
    `the contract`                                      IS A `Contract facts`
    `the misrepresentation`                             IS A `Misrepresentation facts`
    `what the insurer would have done`                  IS A `What the insurer would have done`
    `the money`                                         IS A `Money facts`

DECLARE `Misrepresentation position` HAS
    `the Act applies`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `qualifying misrepresentation`                      IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `class`                                             IS A MAYBE `Class of misrepresentation`
    `remedy`                                            IS A MAYBE `Remedy`

@ref ss 1-5, 12(4), Sch 1 Part 1
@export default The position under the Consumer Insurance (Disclosure and Representations) Act 2012 (UK) when a consumer made a misrepresentation before taking out insurance: whether the Act applies (ss 1, 12(4)); if it does, whether the misrepresentation is a qualifying one (s 4), its class if so (s 5: deliberate or reckless, or careless), and what the insurer may do (Schedule 1 Part 1). The last three are NOTHING when the Act does not apply, and the class is NOTHING when the misrepresentation does not qualify. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Misrepresentation case`  @desc The contract, the misrepresentation and what the consumer knew, what the insurer would have done, and the premiums and claim
GIVETH A `Misrepresentation position`
`the misrepresentation position for` c MEANS
    `Misrepresentation position` WITH
        `the Act applies`                               IS applies
        `qualifying misrepresentation`                  IS IF applies THEN JUST qualifying ELSE NOTHING
        `class`                                         IS IF applies AND qualifying THEN JUST (`the class of` m) ELSE NOTHING
        `remedy`                                        IS IF applies THEN JUST (`the insurer's remedy for` k `and` m `given` w `and` x) ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        k MEANS c's `the contract`
        m MEANS c's `the misrepresentation`
        w MEANS c's `what the insurer would have done`
        x MEANS c's `the money`
        applies MEANS `the Act applies to` k
        qualifying MEANS `is a qualifying misrepresentation` m `given` w `and` x
